      evolution: `From cotton mills to steel to autos to hotels to airlines to software to consumer to power to defense. Tata Sons, the holding company, is owned largely by charitable trusts \u2014 profits recirculate into education, healthcare, and research. Almost no other group of this size is structured this way.`,
      today: `100+ operating companies, ~$150B+ in group revenue, ~1M+ employees, and a market cap that would rank as a top-15 nation\u2019s GDP. Tata brought back Air India in 2022 \u2014 the airline that Tata originally founded in 1932 and lost to nationalization in 1953. Full circle.`,
      whatsNext: `Semiconductors (Tata Electronics), EVs (Tata Motors passenger cars are already the country\u2019s EV leader), and digital \u2014 Tata Neu app, Air India digital reinvention. The next century may look less like a group of companies and more like an operating system for modern India.`,
