      evolution: `From co-op to brand to national FMCG player. Kurien\u2019s Operation Flood turned India from milk-deficient to the world\u2019s largest milk producer. Amul now competes with Nestl\u00e9, Unilever, Britannia \u2014 all foreign, all better-funded \u2014 and quietly outsells them across most categories.`,
      today: `~$8B revenue, ~50M households served daily, ~3.6M farmer-owners. Amul is India\u2019s largest food company by revenue and often by market share. Every second Indian consumer has an Amul product in their fridge. And every rupee flows back to villages.`,
