      failuresAndPivots: `A trading platform outage during a major market event in 2020 cost customers real money and did serious brand damage. The Kamaths owned it publicly, refunded users, and rebuilt infrastructure. In a category where trust is oxygen, the response mattered more than the failure.`,
      evolution: `From discount broker to investing platform to ecosystem. Rainmatter has quietly seeded dozens of Indian fintech and health startups. Varsity teaches millions to invest for free. And Zerodha itself, still bootstrapped, is worth billions \u2014 with founders who own it outright.`,
      today: `~14M+ clients \u2014 India\u2019s largest broker. \u20B92,900 Cr profit in FY23. Zero venture capital, zero advertising, zero acquisition addiction. Zerodha is a case study in how compounding, restraint, and product quality can beat a category full of much better-funded competitors.`,
      whatsNext: `The regulatory landscape is shifting \u2014 new margin rules, F&O tightening, and possibly caps on retail derivatives. Zerodha must expand into wealth management, mutual funds (Coin), and long-hold investing without breaking the low-friction culture. And Rainmatter may quietly become the story.`,
