      problem: `Every internet business in India was leaking money at checkout. The dominant gateways monetized dysfunction \u2014 slow, hard-to-integrate, unreliable. Developers had no voice in the ecosystem.`,
      spark: `Harshil and Shashank\u2019s insight: treat payments as a developer product, not a bank product. Ship an API a solo founder could integrate in an evening. Ship docs that just worked. Ship a dashboard that a non-engineer could operate. Everything the incumbents assumed didn\u2019t matter, made all the difference.`,
      firstMVP: `A single API endpoint and a Stripe-inspired dashboard. Launched from Y Combinator in 2015. Small merchants integrated in hours instead of weeks. Word spread through Indian dev communities and hackathons. Twelve months in, thousands of small businesses were live \u2014 mostly because their friends had recommended it.`,
