      evolution: `From payment gateway to payment stack to banking layer (RazorpayX) to lending (Capital) to POS (Ezetap) to cross-border. Razorpay is quietly becoming the operating system that Indian SMEs run their money on \u2014 a category equivalent to Stripe + Brex + Square combined, tuned for Indian rails.`,
      today: `~10M+ businesses use Razorpay. Millions of small merchants who could not have sold online five years ago can now do so with a few lines of code. Razorpay is one of the highest-valued private fintechs in India and a poster child for the country\u2019s SaaS-to-fintech pipeline.`,
      whatsNext: `Cross-border payments (Southeast Asia expansion), embedded finance for platforms, and AI-driven risk and lending. As Indian SMBs move online, Razorpay could become their default finance stack. The regulatory question \u2014 how much a private fintech can own of the banking value chain \u2014 will define the ceiling.`,
